:"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"C043\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States Rule 6c-11 is available to open-end management investment company ETFs and does not cover UIT ETFs.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Says leveraged and inverse ETFs are eligible and that leveraged/inverse status alone does not require separate relief. Notes they must comply with Rule 18f-4 (derivatives risk program, VaR limits, reporting) unless the limited-user exception applies.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Covers non-transparent/semi-transparent ETFs and share-class ETFs needing separate exemptive relief, and names daily holdings disclosure as a condition. Omits master-feeder structures, so the bundle is incomplete.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"There is no central error: leveraged/inverse ETFs are not excluded, UITs are not treated as covered, and nontransparent and share-class ETFs are correctly said to need separate relief. No material local falsehood was found. Points 1 and 2 are fully covered, but point 3 omits master-feeder structures. Total coverage is 2.5 of 3, which meets the partial threshold but not correct, since correct requires every required minimum.\"}","ttft_ms":3791,"type":"result","duration_ms":7070,"uuid":"820a6e27-d997-4bd2-aeba-5dce9623eca3","ttft_stream_ms":1558,"time_to_request_ms":72,"first_content_frame_ms":1558,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
